.TH SYS_ACPI 2
.SH NAME
sys_acpi \- the firmware's ACPI tables, for drivers (SYS_ACPI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include "mk.h"

long sys_acpi(void *buf, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sys_acpi
copies the firmware's ACPI tables into
.IR buf ,
one after the other: the FADT, the DSDT, then each SSDT (up to 64
tables), each with its own header and length. The AML interpreter
(user/lib/aml.c) reads them: the ACPI server
.BR acpid (4)
for power, battery, lid and sleep, and the touchpad server
.BR i2chid (4)
for its devices.
.PP
If
.I size
is smaller than all the tables together, nothing is copied and their
total size is returned: call again with a buffer that big.
.PP
x86-64 only; drivers only.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The total size of the tables in bytes, or a negative error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EPERM
The caller is not a driver.
.TP
.B ENOSYS
No ACPI (arm64).
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I buf
is not writable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_fdt (2),
.BR sys_power (2),
.BR acpid (4)
